=== TITLE: USG Cranial / Neurosonogram (Neonate) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NORMAL TRANSFONTANELLAR NEONATAL CRANIAL ULTRASOUND STUDY.
- Normal ventricular size and symmetry without midline shift.
- No intraventricular or germinal matrix hemorrhage (Grade 0).

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: TRANSFONTANELLAR NEONATAL CRANIAL ULTRASONOGRAPHY

OBSERVATIONS:
- VENTRICULAR SYSTEM: Lateral ventricles, third ventricle, and fourth ventricle are normal in size, shape, and symmetrical. No ventriculomegaly or hydrocephalus.
- CAUDOTHALAMIC GROOVES & GERMINAL MATRIX: Smooth and clear bilaterally. No subependymal or germinal matrix hemorrhage noted.
- CHOROID PLEXUSES: Normal and symmetrical in echogenicity without cysts or intraventricular clot.
- BRAIN PARENCHYMA: Periventricular white matter demonstrates normal uniform echogenicity without periventricular leukomalacia (PVL).
- MIDLINE STRUCTURES: Corpus callosum, cavum septum pellucidum, and cerebellum appear normal in morphology. Midline echo is central.